Plain setup for players who have never used Xcode, Local signing only, and the weekly renewal.

Brighter Pocket Companion (the management app) and the app's library, reviewed as a player
who has never used Xcode, a free Apple Account, and an install that fails partway:
- This Mac comes before the Apple Account step (signing in needs Xcode), with Get Xcode
  wherever Xcode is missing; Xcode's first launch and the sign-in are numbered steps; the
  build helper (XcodeGen) installs itself; a Free Up Space button.
- The Apple Account step speaks to a free account first; a team ID only behind "I have a
  paid membership"; the paid membership an optional note.
- Local signing only: no Developer service choice, VPN or tunnel text anywhere a player sees,
  and the mode always Local signing (pocket/layer.env preselects it; the library hides its
  mode chooser in a build that preselects one).
- A signature that runs out within two days is Install not done: a banner on the first screen
  with Renew Pocket, which builds again; "Keep it working" says 7 days or a year.
- Diagnosis: the narrow causes first (a free account's 3 apps, 10 App IDs a week, Xcode's iOS
  download, an expired profile, an untrusted developer, a locked or unreachable device); the
  Personal Team rule never for a team already known to be free; a plain line, Report a
  Problem and Copy Details for a failure no rule knows.
- A Trust step for free accounts; the keychain prompt explained while it shows; Steam, not
  Battle.net; Install in Steam (steam://install); "Pocket", the Home Screen name, in the
  steps; the library's empty state points to the companion's Copy step.
Upstream note: Brighter Pocket's own; Tolkara's management keeps its general wording.

